## How to use my NTP server

Point your NTP client to, preferably, `dreamstation.systems`. If your NTP client is IP‐only, you can hardcode `67.215.249.229`. Unfortunately currently IPv4‐only, my VPS provider lives in the stone age.

We serve NTP on 123/UDP, as well as NTS-KE on 4460/TCP using a Let's Encrypt certificate.

We use chrony {!html:"}`ratelimit interval 2 burst 32`{!html:"}: burst of 32 requests, refilling 1 per 4 seconds per source IP. Your packets will be dropped if you exceed this. This should be more than enough for single clients and small NATs. Please do not hardcode `dreamstation.systems` on every host in a large NAT; use `pool.ntp.org`.

If you are a vendor, please do not hardcode `dreamstation.systems` in your devices; use [a NTP pool vendor zone](https://www.ntppool.org/en/vendors.html#vendor-zone).

Please never use `dreamstation.systems` for safety‐critical systems.

## About the time we serve

We do {html:**not**}{!html:*not*} do leap smearing. Leap seconds are handled per RFC 5905.

